From 891bf1b3316e88879d2907afb9f18f0a6df78ff8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Miroslav=20Mr=C3=A1z?= <miroslav.mraz@techmania.cz>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 00:28:07 +0200
Subject: [PATCH v1] drm/msm/adreno: add SM7125 A618 speed-bin 159
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The Adreno 618 in SM7125 (atoll) - e.g. the Samsung Galaxy A52 4G
(samsung,a52q) - is fused to GPU speed-bin 159, which none of the
existing A618 entries describe. It shares the 0x06010800 chip-id with
sc7180 and sm7150, so it is otherwise matched by the generic
(no .machine) A618 entry. That entry lists only the sc7180 bins
(0/169/174) and carries no clock gating, so on SM7125 the unknown bin
makes the driver enable every OPP including the 825 MHz TURBO_L1
corner, and hardware clock gating is left disabled. The GPU then fails
to come up ("missing support for speed-bin: 159", adreno_idle
ringbuffer drain timeout, "gpu hw init failed: -22", GMU faults /
"failed to power off SPTPRAC").

Add a dedicated .machine = "qcom,sm7125" entry, mirroring the existing
sm7150 one: same chip-id, a615 hwcg, a615_zap.mbn and speed-bin 159
mapped to opp-supported-hw bit 3. Bin 159 corresponds to a 750 MHz
(NOM_L1) FMAX per the downstream atoll fuse mapping (FMAX/4.8 + 2,
rounded up).

Using a per-SoC entry rather than extending the shared generic A618
entry keeps hwcg and the new bin scoped to SM7125 and leaves the
sc7180 chromebooks (bins 0/169/174) unchanged.

Based on the sm7125-mainline tree work by Vitalii Skorkin
<nikroks@mainlining.org>.
Signed-off-by: Miroslav Mráz <miroslav.mraz@techmania.cz>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_catalog.c | 25 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 25 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_catalog.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_catalog.c
index 90a0c7ffb3c8..83e5b1f49692 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_catalog.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_catalog.c
@@ -785,6 +785,31 @@ static const struct adreno_info a6xx_gpus[] = {
 			{ 167, 3 },
 			{ 172, 4 },
 		),
+	}, {
+		.machine = "qcom,sm7125",
+		.chip_ids = ADRENO_CHIP_IDS(0x06010800),
+		.family = ADRENO_6XX_GEN1,
+		.revn = 618,
+		.fw = {
+			[ADRENO_FW_SQE] = "a630_sqe.fw",
+			[ADRENO_FW_GMU] = "a630_gmu.bin",
+		},
+		.gmem = SZ_512K,
+		.inactive_period = DRM_MSM_INACTIVE_PERIOD,
+		.quirks = ADRENO_QUIRK_HAS_CACHED_COHERENT |
+			  ADRENO_QUIRK_4GB_VA,
+		.funcs = &a6xx_gpu_funcs,
+		.zapfw = "a615_zap.mbn",
+		.a6xx = &(const struct a6xx_info) {
+			.hwcg = a615_hwcg,
+			.protect = &a630_protect,
+			.gmu_cgc_mode = 0x00000222,
+			.prim_fifo_threshold = 0x00180000,
+		},
+		.speedbins = ADRENO_SPEEDBINS(
+			{ 0,   0 },
+			{ 159, 3 },
+		),
 	}, {
 		.chip_ids = ADRENO_CHIP_IDS(0x06010800),
 		.family = ADRENO_6XX_GEN1,

